{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353705-contemplating-a-house-rule","id":1353705,"title":"Contemplating a house rule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-08T22:39:04-08:00","id":1353705,"title":"Contemplating a house rule","content":"To reduce the feeling that players <i>must</i> buy their Arete up to two dots in order to be able to really do anything with their magick, and because Exalted 3E has a rule I really like (it's page 179, &quot;Raising Essence,&quot; if you want to go read it), I'm considering the following houserule:<br /> <br /> Arete starts at \u2022\u2022 for new characters, but cannot be improved directly, either with freebie points during chargen or with XP during play. Instead, PC mages become eligible for Seekings when they have grown as people (spent a certain amount of experience), according to the following table:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">50xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">100xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">150xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">225xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">300xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">400xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">500xp</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">600xp</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T23:56:54-08:00","id":1353721,"title":"","content":"I think you might want to consider something to make up for the fact that a lot of starting concepts are going to want a Sphere at 3 which would be impossible under this scheme.<br /> <br /> Otherwise it's a fine idea, though you might want to increase the values a bit more drastically. Arete 6+ is a huge game changer that most games don't get into because Arete costs a lot of XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T11:20:27-08:00","id":1353907,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd dial the barriers way higher. 1000xp is considered Oracle level, so really a good point for 10. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 150px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">100 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">250 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">400 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">550 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">700 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">850 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1000 XP</td> </tr> </table></div> Arete 4 takes 100 Xp. After that, every Arete increase has an XP barrier in 150xp steps. I'd still make Arete 6+ optional, but if people wanna go higher, adjust the handing out out of XP accordingly - but not too much. It should take a long, long time.<br /> For playing an intentionally earlier high level game of epic proportions, one could start with Arete 6 at the top of the table at 250xp and do the 150xp steps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T15:54:32-08:00","id":1353984,"title":"","content":"I start Arete at 2 but require 7 rather than 4 freebie points to raise Arete to 3. That way the freebie cost is proportional to the XP cost for it. And the max is still 3 starting out.<br /> <br /> Making the costs really high might make sense in terms of the amount of time in-game it actually takes to raise it, but I think there is an expectation in roleplaying games that advancement is faster than &quot;real life&quot; or even what is typical for NPC's in the setting. Maybe your players are more understanding than mine. I know if I used your XP costs with my players they would be upset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 12-09-2019, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T16:47:42-08:00","id":1353996,"title":"","content":"Note, Faradn - these are not XP *costs*.<br /> These are the total amounts of XP gained (and used for other things) before the characters can go on seekings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T17:32:09-08:00","id":1354012,"title":"","content":"I would do the automatic Arete to 5 and then require XP purchases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T20:34:39-08:00","id":1354054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353705-contemplating-a-house-rule?p=1353907#post1353907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'd dial the barriers way higher. 1000xp is considered Oracle level, so really a good point for 10. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 150px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">100 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">250 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">400 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">550 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">700 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">850 XP</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Arete 10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1000 XP</td> </tr> </table></div> Arete 4 takes 100 Xp. After that, every Arete increase has an XP barrier in 150xp steps. I'd still make Arete 6+ optional, but if people wanna go higher, adjust the handing out out of XP accordingly - but not too much. It should take a long, long time.<br /> For playing an intentionally earlier high level game of epic proportions, one could start with Arete 6 at the top of the table at 250xp and do the 150xp steps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This more or less tracks with my own Mage game where all the characters began as Arete 3 mages. We've been playing about 9-10 years IRL (though we've slowed down <i>quite</i> a bit in the past four or five years as everyone's crested their early- to mid-30's) and all the PC's have around 255-270 XP, and I'm allowing them to Seek for Arete 5 at the end of the current story. Obviously I have no bases upon which to say I did it the right way, or that where you drew the bright lines is more or less right than any other arbitrary numbers--but I did want to mention that I can at least vouch for this having happened more or less organically in my own game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T22:56:40-08:00","id":1354313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353705-contemplating-a-house-rule?p=1353996#post1353996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, Faradn - these are not XP *costs*.<br /> These are the total amounts of XP gained (and used for other things) before the characters can go on seekings.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T06:03:44-08:00","id":1354560,"title":"","content":"Conversely, I've always been a fan of <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s Arcane Experience: you get two pools of experience, one for regular stuff and one for Arcane stuff; you can only spend your Arcane Experience to improve arcane traits. <br /> <br /> In <b>Mage: the Ascension</b>, I'd implement this as \u201cFocal Experience\u201d: bonus XP that are awarded above and beyond the usual XP awards for properly roleplaying your Paradigm and/or Avatar Essence, and that can be spent on Arete, Spheres, your Practice's associated Abilities, and appropriate supernatural Merits and Backgrounds (things like Dream and Arcane). Arete (and possibly some supernatural Merits and Backgrounds) would <i>only</i> be improvable using Focal XPs; Spheres and Practice-associated Abilities would be improvable by both. <br /> <br /> During character creation, start everyone at Arete 2, and give them enough \u201cFocal Freebies\u201d (Freebie Points that can be spent on the same things that Focal XPs can be spent on) to buy a third dot if they want to \u2014 or let them \u201csell off\u201d an Arete dot for more Focal Freebies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T10:53:57-08:00","id":1354615,"title":"","content":"Splat XP is certainly worth looking at to port over to the WoD, but I'm not sure I'd like it here.<br /> <br /> To me, one of the reasons to switch to this for Ascension, is that Seekings can fail. Putting an XP cost on Arete, and a Seeking failing, is a huge unfun moment (so bad I've seen STs bend over backwards into five knots to avoid it). Qualifying for a Seeking in this sort of scheme (though looking at Scion's Legend increase is a different non-XP gated option along the same lines) means you can fail a Seeking with far less worry, since you can just try again soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:02:00-08:00","id":1354636,"title":"","content":"<s>Note that I said that*</s> you need to be able to pay for the dot in order to attempt a Seeking, not that you must pay for it first. Attempt your Seeking, succeed, <i>then</i> buy the dot.<br /> <br /> My thought on this would be that if you fail a Seeking, there's a reason for it; and you must somehow address whatever shortcoming you had that caused the failure before you can try again. In the meantime, those Focal XPs can be kept in reserve for another attempt, or they can be spent on other things if you don't think you're going to be ready for another try any time soon. Either way, they're not wasted.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:gray\">* Oops; I didn't say that; it was from an earlier draft that somehow got cut. Sorry about that.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-12-2019, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T15:47:29-08:00","id":1354689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1353705-contemplating-a-house-rule?p=1354615#post1354615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splat XP is certainly worth looking at to port over to the WoD, but I'm not sure I'd like it here.<br /> <br /> To me, one of the reasons to switch to this for Ascension, is that Seekings can fail. Putting an XP cost on Arete, and a Seeking failing, is a huge unfun moment (so bad I've seen STs bend over backwards into five knots to avoid it). Qualifying for a Seeking in this sort of scheme (though looking at Scion's Legend increase is a different non-XP gated option along the same lines) means you can fail a Seeking with far less worry, since you can just try again soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2E I remember you lose half the XP you would have spent if you fail a Seeking, but I didn't see anything about that in Revised and I looked pretty hard for it. Is that how it works in M20?<br /> <br /> Regardless, the way I do Seekings it's more of a learning experience than a pass/fail sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}